> >5. What stuff is safe to eat ?????
> >
> Oh my.  I'll let someone else answer this question.

I'll give it a poke.  Probably the most important intrinsic to gain
early on in the game is poison resistance, unless you're a barbarian or
healer (who start with it).  Unfortunately, unless you've found a ton of
restore ability potions or have a unicorn horn handy, you have to find
non-toxic monsters to eat to get it.  The ones I know of that are safe
to eat and can give you poison resistance are quivering blobs (these
seem to have the best chance, since I think they're the highest level of
this lot), cave spiders, shriekers and all of the molds except for
yellow mold (poisonous and hallucinagenic) and violet mold
(hallucinagenic, but if you don't mind that go for it).  Watch out: 
green mold is acidic, and causes you damage when you eat it, so be
careful (I've snuffed it from noshing acidic corpses).

Sleep resistance can be conferred by eating elves (do NOT eat the
corpses left by elf zombies, unless you like being terminally ill) or
acid blobs.  Once again, watch out for the acid blobs, they're acidic
(duh).

Cold, fire, shock and disintegration resistance can be conferred by
pretty much any creature that uses these as a form of attack.  In
addition, brown molds can give cold resistance, red molds can give fire
resistance, and the puddings (brown and black) as well as gelatinous
cubes can give tons of intrinsics (all of the above save disintegration,
I believe).  Black dragons are the only creature I know of that can
confer disintegration resistance.

Intrinsic teleportation can be conferred by leprachauns, nymphs and
tengus, which is a pain in the ass unless you can get intrinsic teleport
control from another tengu (or from eating the Wizard of Yendor, but see
below).

Telepathy can be gained from eating a floating eye, and it's automatic.

Aggrivate monster can be gained by eating any human ("@") including
were-creatures but excluding elves (unless you're playing an elf, in
which case I believe these are reversed).  So, you can gain intrinsic
teleportation control from the wizard of Yendor, but it will also give
you aggrivate monster.

Any that I missed?

